WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.180
&gt;&gt; Hi, my name is

00:00:24.181 --> 00:00:27.505
Anande and I'll talking
about Resource Central.

00:00:27.506 --> 00:00:30.255
We are exploring ways to create

00:00:30.256 --> 00:00:33.050
intelligent and efficient
cloud platforms.

00:00:33.051 --> 00:00:36.090
To do this, we want
to leverage machine

00:00:36.091 --> 00:00:39.450
learning into the cloud platform
resource management.

00:00:39.451 --> 00:00:42.350
There are several research
challenges like,

00:00:42.351 --> 00:00:44.060
how can we make this machine

00:00:44.061 --> 00:00:46.770
learning integration
generic enough?

00:00:46.771 --> 00:00:48.830
So, the idea is to put

00:00:48.831 --> 00:00:52.280
Resource Central right
into the center of Azure.

00:00:52.281 --> 00:00:57.760
As you see here, various
resource management services in

00:00:57.761 --> 00:00:59.370
the cloud platform conduct

00:00:59.371 --> 00:01:00.950
Resource Central and get

00:01:00.951 --> 00:01:04.000
predictions about
the future behaviors.

00:01:04.001 --> 00:01:06.650
So, Resource Central is

00:01:06.651 --> 00:01:09.530
a general platform for
collecting telemetry,

00:01:09.531 --> 00:01:11.705
learning about
the prior behaviors of

00:01:11.706 --> 00:01:14.480
VMs and servers and
when requested,

00:01:14.481 --> 00:01:18.200
it can produce predictions
of the future behavior.

00:01:18.201 --> 00:01:21.370
We have some highlights here.

00:01:21.371 --> 00:01:24.570
We had a paper in
SOSP17 about this.

00:01:24.571 --> 00:01:27.290
The Resource Central service
is currently in

00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:30.250
production in Azure
compute fabric.

00:01:30.251 --> 00:01:33.790
Here, we can see the architecture
of Resource Central,

00:01:33.791 --> 00:01:35.755
there are two main parts of it.

00:01:35.756 --> 00:01:39.025
There is offline processing
where you collect telemetry,

00:01:39.026 --> 00:01:41.830
you create machine-learning
generated models,

00:01:41.831 --> 00:01:45.845
and there is an online
serving platform which allows

00:01:45.846 --> 00:01:48.410
the resource managers
to make queries

00:01:48.411 --> 00:01:51.950
to Resource Central
and serve predictions.

00:01:51.951 --> 00:01:55.495
As you can see, with
Resource Central,

00:01:55.496 --> 00:01:56.975
we can predict with

00:01:56.976 --> 00:02:01.220
a high quality various
metrics of workloads.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.500
That is a strong reason
to integrate

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:06.880
machine-learning in resource
management in platforms.

00:02:06.881 --> 00:02:09.500
Here we have some future machine

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.715
learning challenges that
we are trying to address,

00:02:11.716 --> 00:02:16.015
for example, online learning
and doing the said skill.

00:02:16.016 --> 00:02:19.700
Now we have a small demo
here which shows

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:22.495
the VM scheduling in Azure

00:02:22.496 --> 00:02:24.590
using Resource Central and

00:02:24.591 --> 00:02:26.420
without using Resource Central.

00:02:26.421 --> 00:02:27.990
So as you can see here,

00:02:27.991 --> 00:02:30.775
without using Resource Central,

00:02:30.776 --> 00:02:34.160
there will be a high probability
of rejections of

00:02:34.161 --> 00:02:37.475
workloads because of
the fixed capacity of the VMs.

00:02:37.476 --> 00:02:40.295
With Resource Central, you get

00:02:40.296 --> 00:02:42.440
informed knowledge about what is

00:02:42.441 --> 00:02:45.115
the kind of work load and
the nature of that workload.

00:02:45.116 --> 00:02:46.655
With that information, you can

00:02:46.656 --> 00:02:49.040
achieve all subscription with

00:02:49.041 --> 00:02:51.770
the same capacity and without

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.945
exhausting the resources
several number of times.

00:02:54.946 --> 00:02:57.270
So, in this approach
without Resource Central,

00:02:57.271 --> 00:02:59.410
you can see there are
a high number of rejections,

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:00.760
whereas with Resource Central,

00:03:00.761 --> 00:03:03.815
the rejections are low
and also that we are

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:08.030
remaining within the capacity
of this all. Thank you.

